{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must be at least 12 characters long.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active PAM/libpwquality configuration sets minlen=12. An 11-character candidate was rejected with the credential unchanged, and the same rejection was observed after restart, while a longer compliant password was accepted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-256863efa0f54e82","cmd-ea143118e4644959","cmd-36dd4132956f4917","cmd-4d359ef6ab31489c","cmd-8267782ecf624ea6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"New user passwords on node1 must use at least three character classes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active policy sets minclass=3. Long two-class candidates were rejected, compliant candidates were accepted, and an exactly-three-class candidate passed after restart. PAM is configured to invoke pam_pwquality.","evidence_ids":["cmd-256863efa0f54e82","cmd-0aa3c40694f34a5a","cmd-6c2259e6c9e7486e","cmd-4d359ef6ab31489c","cmd-8267782ecf624ea6","cmd-238d0df50ccd4b8b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were observed before and after execution, including after a verified restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d403ca094cb24a96","cmd-09dab7afa5bf431c","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation uses the installed RHEL PAM, libpwquality, authselect, and shadow-utils components. Authselect remained valid, package verification showed no reported damage, and final package health was successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d403ca094cb24a96","cmd-ea143118e4644959","cmd-4bf705022bce4950","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"State changes were narrowly tied to the policy, bounded behavioral testing, cleanup, or the mandatory restart protocol. The temporary test account, secret, and probe files were removed, account-database checksums returned to baseline, SELinux remained enforcing, no failed services or new listeners appeared, and package health remained good. One minor unnecessary mutation occurred: cmd-2d77c43a09454a0e created temporary probe output files during a failed validation attempt caused by the absent openssl command; it contributed no valid result but removed those files within the same command, leaving no residue. No other unnecessary mutation was identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-65f653792bd74ec5","cmd-2d77c43a09454a0e","cmd-93996184bdbb49f7","cmd-0b149b22c40e4501","cmd-4bf705022bce4950","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The password policy is durably integrated with the existing PAM stack and directly demonstrated to reject passwords shorter than 12 characters or using fewer than three classes. The OS release and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, a different boot ID was observed, and services, policy behavior, account data, and platform state recovered successfully.","limitations":["The passwd --stdin probes sometimes returned exit code 0 for rejected administrative changes; rejection is established instead by direct before/after credential-hash equality. This exit-code behavior slightly reduces evidentiary clarity.","No full package transaction history was captured, although matching pre/post platform versions, unchanged relevant package versions, successful RPM verification, and healthy DNF state strongly support platform preservation.","The exactly-three-class acceptance probe used pwscore/libpwquality rather than completing a real PAM credential change; PAM integration and compliant credential-change behavior were demonstrated separately.","Restart evidence is otherwise complete and corroborated by the fixed boot-identity snapshots: 050a5b4c-6c7b-42ad-957a-b6a41a0d34db before execution and b15398f5-0f20-478d-969e-c21d19f51e5b afterward."]}
